{"id":"da6e3d3afda6cce6","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-shoenfield.md","title":"Shoenfield Absoluteness","display":"thm-shoenfield — Shoenfield Absoluteness","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-shoenfield","aliases":["58-thm-shoenfield"],"display":"thm-shoenfield — Shoenfield Absoluteness","depends_on":["[[58-df-formula]]","[[58-df-transitive]]","[[58-df-satisfaction]]","[[58-df-proper]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-shoenfield"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-shoenfield</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-shoenfield — Shoenfield Absoluteness"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2d9fd66bae7ead5a\" href=\"?note=2d9fd66bae7ead5a\" title=\"58-df-transitive\">58-df-transitive</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"58-df-satisfaction\">58-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"8935dcac821c0104\" href=\"?note=8935dcac821c0104\" title=\"58-df-proper\">58-df-proper</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,N,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,r,\\varphi\\in V\">\\(M,N,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,r,\\varphi\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Transitive}\">\\(\\mathrm{Transitive}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Model}\">\\(\\mathrm{Model}\\)</span> are the exact set/model predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZFC}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\)</span> is the coded first-order set theory.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\lor\\Pi^1_2(\\varphi,r)\">\\(\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\lor\\Pi^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\)</span> means that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\">\\(\\varphi\\)</span> is a coded projective formula with real parameter <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r\">\\(r\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\varphi,r)\">\\(\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\varphi,r)\\)</span> means truth of that second-order-arithmetic formula in the standard naturals and reals as computed by the transitive model <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}shoenfield\\text{-}absoluteness}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{Transitive}(M)\\land\\mathrm{Transitive}(N)\\land M\\subseteq N\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathfrak M,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathfrak N,N)\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathfrak M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathfrak N,\\mathrm{ZFC})\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land(\\operatorname{Ord}\\cap M)=(\\operatorname{Ord}\\cap N)\n\\land r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\n\\land\\bigl(\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\lor\\Pi^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\longrightarrow\\left(\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\varphi,r)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(N,\\varphi,r)\n\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}shoenfield\\text{-}absoluteness}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{Transitive}(M)\\land\\mathrm{Transitive}(N)\\land M\\subseteq N\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathfrak M,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathfrak N,N)\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathfrak M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathfrak N,\\mathrm{ZFC})\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land(\\operatorname{Ord}\\cap M)=(\\operatorname{Ord}\\cap N)\n\\land r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\n\\land\\bigl(\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\lor\\Pi^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\longrightarrow\\left(\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\varphi,r)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(N,\\varphi,r)\n\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The common-ordinal and real-parameter hypotheses prevent the unrestricted-model overstatement in the former version.</li>\n<li>ZFC is now applied to explicit membership-structure codes, while projective truth is correctly marked as a second-order-arithmetic metatheoretic relation.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-transitive","status":"resolved","id":"2d9fd66bae7ead5a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-transitive]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-satisfaction","status":"resolved","id":"8b6a90316aad78a4","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-satisfaction]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-proper","status":"resolved","id":"8935dcac821c0104","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-proper]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M,N,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak N,r,\\varphi\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Transitive}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Model}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZFC}","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\lor\\Pi^1_2(\\varphi,r)","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"r","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\varphi,r)","display":false},{"tex":"M","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}shoenfield\\text{-}absoluteness}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{Transitive}(M)\\land\\mathrm{Transitive}(N)\\land M\\subseteq N\\\\\n&\\quad\\land\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathfrak M,M)\n\\land\\mathrm{MembershipStructure}_S(\\mathfrak N,N)\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathfrak M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathfrak N,\\mathrm{ZFC})\\\\\n&\\quad\\land(\\operatorname{Ord}\\cap M)=(\\operatorname{Ord}\\cap N)\n\\land r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\n\\land\\bigl(\\Sigma^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\lor\\Pi^1_2(\\varphi,r)\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\quad\\longrightarrow\\left(\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\varphi,r)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(N,\\varphi,r)\n\\right).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":1870,"backlinks":[{"id":"9a2fb66895acc799","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ProjectiveTruth}_{\\mathsf{meta}}$ is the metatheoretic projective-truth relation used in [[58-thm-shoenfield]]."},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4418","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-thm-shoenfield.md|58-thm-shoenfield]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["65418b505fc53093","2d9fd66bae7ead5a","8b6a90316aad78a4","8935dcac821c0104"]}